Z||000008||fieroburton||08-10-2001||12:37 AM||||no fiero owners don't wave we flick off  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I'm just joking fiero owners are very nice.<P>------------------<BR>1984 2M4 SE <BR>    [img]www.geocities.com/fieroburton/25_25.jpg[/img]<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fieroburton/1.html" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fieroburton/1.html</A>||||reg||12
Z||000009||TN Fieros||08-10-2001||12:41 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LT1 Chop Top:<BR><B>When I ride my motorcycle, most rider wave too, usually not Harley owners.......they have to hang on due to excessive vibration and fear of falling off.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>heheh.. that's not it... we're just motorcycle snobs! Just like when I was driving my 911 Porsches. You always wave at 911 drivers, sometimes 928 drivers and never 944 or 914 drivers. Not that there is anything wrong with those cars.. that's just how it is..<P>Actually riding with one hand is something that a lot of Harley riders too... just for the fact that it is dangerous and makes you look tough. Just think of the old suicide shift Harleys that had a foot clutch and a gear shift coming up and attaching to the side of the tank. Now that's a man's motorcycle!<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TNFiero[1].gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Songman||08-10-2001||12:42 AM||||Who is this TN Fiero guy that is posting my responses anyway?!?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/icons/icon12.gif"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000011||FieroKyle||08-10-2001||01:49 AM||||I always wave and if I see other Fieros at a gas station or where ever, I try to make a trip to talk to them or see their car. A lot of times when I wave, I almost always wave to a non-Fiero enthuasist thats driving a Fiero, or its some really old chunky lady in one, then they give me a funny look like I am fricken retard. Sorry, just my luck, lol. I have run into people who do enjoy there cars though. One night I stopped to talk to a guy at a McDonalds parking lot, unfortunatly he was waiting for a tow there because of Fiero over heating problems. It was a 85' GT.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Black88GT||08-10-2001||02:42 AM||||For whatever reason, I am always in a different car when I see another Fiero around here.  I dunno why that is.  But, if I am on the highway and I get a trucker next to me (usually heavier traffic times) I can look up at them through the pass. side t-top.  They always smile and wave.  ||||reg||1
Z||000013||artherd||08-10-2001||05:19 AM||||I always wave if I see an intresting car, any intresting car :) Corvette, porsche, ferrari (of course) lambo, musclecar, dude on a motorcycle, etc.<P>Oh, fieros too of course, sometimes I'll stalk fieros, ferraris and lambos (follow them to gas stations even though my tank is full, etc :)  Sometimes end up talking with the fieros, fun fun!!<P><BR>So do we wave, heck yes! ;)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000014||AusFiero||08-10-2001||09:33 AM||||Some Pontiac owners wave to me. But with 260,000 people in town and only 1 other Fiero, which I never see. I reckon I would give chase. Seen another one of the only 3 t-topped Fieros in Australia the other day, shame I wasn't in mine. I think he woulda got a little worried if I gave chase in the Commodore being an ex cop car and all.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000015||LZeitgeist||08-10-2001||09:59 AM||||I stopped waving when the stupid looks I got back vs. the return waves reached about a 2000:1 ratio. <P>Evidently there are only two Fiero enthusiasts in Raleigh NC that drive their cars every day, and a third who doesn't drive his all that much - and all three of us already know each other. *sigh*  <P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001||||reg||1
